libmidas for Debian
-------------------

This is the SDL 1.2 port of MIDAS Digital Audio System 1.1.2 (2000). It plays
MOD, S3M, XM and IT modules.

The upstream code was written for 32-bit systems. The Debian patches make it
work on 64-bit architectures (amd64, arm64...): before them, MIDASinit()
crashed and no module could be loaded.

Known upstream limitation: IT modules whose samples are compressed (Impulse
Tracker 2.14 compression, used by recent trackers) are not supported. Loading
them fails with "Unexpected end of file".

Programs using this library must be compiled with -fpack-struct, like the
library itself, if they use the structures of midasdll.h.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>, reviewed by Nicolas HOUDELOT.

